{"id":"global-village-coffeehouse","title":"Global Village Coffeehouse","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Global_Village_Coffeehouse","rev":239609,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse"]}," (GVC) is a design aesthetic that was prevalent from the late 1980s to the early 2000s. It emerged as a reaction against the sleeker, tech-oriented styles of the mid-late 1980s, such as ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Lite"],"id":"memphis-lite"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Laser Grid"],"id":"laser-grid"},", reflecting a shift to a more environmental and nature-oriented style. The term was coined by Evan Collins of ",{"t":"a","c":["CARI"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Consumer_Aesthetics_Research_Institute"},". GVC was succeeded by the ",{"t":"a","c":["Mission School"],"id":"mission-school"}," aesthetic in the late 1990s and early 2000s."]},{"t":"p","c":["The GVC aesthetic is defined by its use of earth tones, rough and recycled textures, and motifs that blend stylized, \"handcrafted\" imagery with a hodgepodge of motifs appropriated from ancient, tribal, and Indigenous cultures. This created a warm, ",{"t":"a","c":["bohemian"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Bohemian"},", and worldly ambiance epitomized by the interior design and branding of chains like Starbucks, Panera Bread, and Barnes & Noble during the 1990s."]},{"t":"p","c":["The style reflected the era's optimistic yet superficial embrace of globalization, \"world music\", and early internet culture, while also being criticized in retrospect for its \"greenwashing\" and \"cultural appropriation\"."]}],"sections":[{"title":"History","id":"history","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse was a sort of reaction against the computer/tech boom of the 1990s. It focused on \"natural\" themes and artificially crafted multiculturalism. This aesthetic emerged in the late 1980s, rose in the early 1990s, and peaked in popularity in the mid-1990s."]},{"t":"p","c":["In late 1990s and early 2000s, GVC began to decline in popularity in favor of the ",{"t":"a","c":["Y2K Futurism"],"id":"y2k-futurism"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Gen X Soft Club"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Gen_X_Soft_Club"}," aesthetics, as the pendulum swung back towards futurism. Industrial and the ",{"t":"a","c":["Mission School"],"id":"mission-school"}," aesthetics came to be perceived as \"more authentic,\" though traces of GVC design continued into the 2000s. Although less popular nowadays, the GVC aesthetic still inspires some interior design, such in as Panera Bread, and occasionally sees use in food packaging."]}]},{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["The visual art style of Global Village Coffeehouse is characterized by its earth tones, detailed woodcut styling, and a use stereotypically \"tribal\" symbols. It overlaps in some aspects with the ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Design"],"id":"memphis-design"}," aesthetic, but with a much more rustic and warm color scheme and geometry, rather than sharp and bold colors. GVC borrows motifs from a wide array of art styles, such as ",{"t":"a","c":["Lowbrow"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Lowbrow"}," (also known as Pop Surrealism), ",{"t":"a","c":["Impressionism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Impressionism"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Cubism"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cubism"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Primitivism"],"href":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primitivism"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Art Deco"],"id":"art-deco"},", and ",{"t":"a","c":["Fauvism"],"href":"https://www.britannica.com/art/Fauvism"},", as well as artists like Chagall, Klimt, Matisse, Picasso."]},{"t":"img","img":{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/dd/XTC.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240703010832","w":180,"h":180,"cap":[{"t":"br"},"XTC - ",{"t":"i","c":["Drums and Wires"]}," (1979)",{"t":"br"},{"t":"a","c":["Pacific Punk Wave"],"id":"pacific-punk-wave"}," designs from the 70s and early 80s often have strikingly GVC-vibes",{"t":"br"}]}},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Elements"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Earth tones"]},{"c":["Airbrushed, \"dirty\" look"]},{"c":["Irregular borders and lines"]},{"c":["Colorful gradated backgrounds"]},{"c":["Horror vacui (a trait common to several other aesthetics of the time)"]},{"c":["A general dislike of expanses of flat colors, which were usually textured in some way"]},{"c":["Layering backgrounds that are misaligned with their line art (also shared with various styles of the era such as ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Lite"],"id":"memphis-lite"},", ",{"t":"a","c":["Shoe Diva"],"id":"shoe-diva"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Mission School"],"id":"mission-school"},")"]},{"c":["Rough, hand-drawn look"],"sub":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Line art with gaps in it, as if sketched"]}]}]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Motifs"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Ancient, petroglyph inspired imagery"]},{"c":["Exoticized traditional African or Native American imagery, including ",{"t":"a","c":["Kokopelli"],"href":"https://www.indigenouspeople.net/kokopelli.htm"}]},{"c":["Keith Haring-style designs (",{"t":"a","c":["Neo-Pop"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Neo-Pop"},")"]},{"c":["Flowing, curvy figures"]},{"c":["Woodcut-style patterns"]},{"c":["Trees, waves, & landscapes"]},{"c":["Coffee cups & aroma swirls"]},{"c":["Moons, Suns, stars, & Earth/globes"]},{"c":["Hands & eyes"]},{"c":["Hearts"]},{"c":["Spirals, squiggles, & drops"],"sub":[{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Reminiscent of ",{"t":"a","c":["Googie"],"href":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Googie"}," motifs, revived by ",{"t":"a","c":["Pacific Punk Wave"],"href":"https://cari.institute/aesthetics/pacific-punk-wave"}," design"]}]}]}]}]},{"title":"Music","id":"music","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse was by and large a graphic and interior design aesthetic; however, its welcoming, multicultural feel-good philosophy was associated with a broader zeitgeist that inspired music that could be considered GVC. Album art and music videos utilized heavily exoticized or appropriated indigenous imagery and new age elements. Much of this overlaps with what could be considered ",{"t":"a","c":["Frasurbane"],"id":"frasurbane"}," or ",{"t":"a","c":["Utopian Scholastic"],"id":"utopian-scholastic"}," music."]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Songs"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["\"Don’t Know Why\" by Norah Jones"]},{"c":["\"Under African Skies\" by Paul Simon"]},{"c":["\"Storms In Africa\" by Enya"]},{"c":["\"Sweet Lullaby\" by Deep Forest"]},{"c":["\"Desert Rose\" by Sting"]},{"c":["\"Kiss of Life\" by Sade"]},{"c":["\"Love Is Stronger Than Pride\" by Sade"]},{"c":["\"Cherish The Day\" by Sade"]},{"c":["\"Sunny Came Home\" by Shawn Calvin"]},{"c":["\"Sadeness - Part I\" by Enigma"]},{"c":["\"Shiny Happy People\" by R.E.M."]},{"c":["\"Hold On\" by Wilson Phillips"]},{"c":["\"Round Here\" by Counting Crows"]},{"c":["\"The Light of the Sun\" by Richie Heaves with Rockapella"]},{"c":["\"Breakfast At Tiffany's\" by Deep Blue Something"]},{"c":["\"Send Me on My Way\" by Rusted Root"]},{"c":["\"In the House of Stone and Light\" by Martin Page"]},{"c":["\"You Oughta Know\" by Alanis Morissette"]},{"c":["\"Runaway\" by Janet Jackson"]},{"c":["\"Together Again\" by Janet Jackson"]},{"c":["\"Sunchyme\" by Dario G"]},{"c":["\"L'argent fait le bonheur\" by Les Respectables"]},{"c":["\"You'll Be in My Heart\" by Phil Collins"]},{"c":["\"I'm Like a Bird\" by Nelly Furtado"]},{"c":["\"The Chase\" by Rednex"]},{"c":["\"Earth Our Home\" by Chet Pinehurst"]},{"c":["\"Earth Funk\" by Zared"]},{"c":["\"Show Me Your Soul\" by Red Hot Chili Peppers"]}]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f6/Rushshow.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20240702171758","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["A Show of Hands"]}," by Rush (1989)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/56/Wecantdance.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701180117","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["We Can't Dance"]}," by Genesis (1991)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/3b/Belcanto.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701180027","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Shimmering, Warm, and Bright"]}," by Bel Canto (1992)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/9b/Hewson.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701180100","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Disappearing Earth"]}," by Dave Hewson (1993)"]}]}]},{"title":"Media","id":"media","blocks":[{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Television & Film"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["When Harry Met Sally"]}," (1989)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Friends"]}," (1994-2004)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Duckman"]}," (1994-1997)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Pocahontas"]}," (1995)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["One Fine Day"]}," (1996)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Big Bag"]}," (Troubles the Cat segments) (1996-1998)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["You've Got Mail"]}," (1998)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Notting Hill"]}," (1999)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Tarzan"]}," (1999)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["A Little Curious"]}," (1999-2000)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Crashbox"]}," (1999-2000)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Gilmore Girls"]}," (2000-2007)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Brother Bear"]}," (2003)"]},{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Chowder"]}," (2007-2010)"]}]},{"t":"h","l":3,"c":["Video Games"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":[{"t":"i","c":["Back to Bed"]}," (2011)"]},{"c":["The Cafe Zone from ",{"t":"i","c":["Hypnospace Outlaw"]}," (2019)"]}]}]},{"title":"Merchandising & Advertisement","id":"merchandising-amp-advertisement","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Elements of Global Village Coffeehouse design were featured in advertisements throughout the 90s. Merchandise, namely food and beverage items, also utilized packaging with these design elements. Although GVC declined in popularity in the early 2000s, some brands still feature these design elements in their branding today."]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/65/Fruitopia.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701181427","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Fruitopia, deisgned"]}," ",{"t":"i","c":["by Replace and Duffy Design"]}," (1995)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/3d/GVC11.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703014054","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Fruitopia, designed"]}," ",{"t":"i","c":["by Replace and Duffy Design"]}," (1995)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/5c/GVC7.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703013122","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Fruitopia"]},", ",{"t":"i","c":["designed by Replace and Duffy Design"]}," (1995)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/87/GVC3.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703012247","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Limited edition Perrier, illustrated"]}," ",{"t":"i","c":["by Burton Morris"]}," (1996)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/01/GVC1.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703012154","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Snapple Elements"]}," (1999)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/46/GVC_Glen_Oaks.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260324215304","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Glen Oaks Farms yogurt, designed by m creative studio and illustrated by Jane Mjolsness"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/7c/Mattarello.png/revision/latest?cb=20240803184153","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Mattarello, designed by Rylands Brand Design"]}," (2015)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/f/f0/Audrey%27s_Chia.png/revision/latest?cb=20240803184152","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Audrey's Chia,"]}," ",{"t":"i","c":["designed"]}," ",{"t":"i","c":["by Brad Ghormlrey"]}," (2019-present)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a7/ABCGVC.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20240816204642","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Alternative Baking Company logo"]}," (90s-present)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/d0/AdobeAcrobat5CDCover.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20230725203229","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Adobe Acrobat 5.0"]}," (2001)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/50/GVC_Nordstrom.png/revision/latest?cb=20260304013312","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Nordstrom Essentials body care"]}," (90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/45/GVC_Paper.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260304013824","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Banana Paper"]}," (90s)"]}]}]},{"title":"Interior Design","id":"interior-design","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Global Village Coffeehouse design was used as inspiration for numerous cafes, restaurants, and bookstores during the 90s, with Starbucks being the most popular. The interior design was made to feel warm and cozy, and included the use of dark wood, earth toned color palettes, and art lining the walls."]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6a/GVC8.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703013141","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Starbucks"]}," (90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/e9/Starbuckscafe.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701181651","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Starbucks"]}," (90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/48/GVC_Starbucks.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260324221643","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Starbucks"]}," (90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/21/GVC_Starbucks_2.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260324221925","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Starbucks"]}," (90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/bc/PeteSahutCoffee.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192528","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Famous Players SilverCity, Mississauga, ON"]}," (1997)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/bd/GVC_Iridium.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260304012153","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Iridium, New York City"]}," (1994)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/2/26/GVC_Split.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260304012611","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Split Rock Bar & Grill, Minneapolis Saint Paul Airport"]}," (90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/7/78/GVC_Fitzcarraldo_Discotheque.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260324222221","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Fitzcarraldo Discotheque designed by Gianni Gavioli"]},", ",{"t":"i","c":["Terranuova Bracciolini, Italy"]}," (1991)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/4b/GVC6.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240703013824","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Suntory's The Earth beer hall, Tokyo"]}," (1990)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1e/GVC4.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703012453","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Suntory's The Earth beer hall, Tokyo"]}," (1990)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/9b/Theearth.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701181444","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Suntory's The Earth beer hall, Tokyo"]}," (1990)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/db/GVC_McDonalds.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260324225358","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["McDonald's on Flatbush Ave, Brooklyn, NY"]}," (90s-Present)"]}]}]},{"title":"Criticism","id":"criticism","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["As a result of increased environmental awareness in the late 1980s, Global Vintage Coffeehouse used imagery inspired by environmentalism. This was meant to brand GVC as down-to-earth and authentic; however, these efforts were seen as insincere, because of its use as a marketing tactic. Similarly, the 1990s brought a fascination with global cultures and new age philosophy. Capitalizing on this led to what GVC has been criticized most for: its use of imagery taken from or inspired by different cultures. This resulted in some viewing it as \"cultural appropriation\" that commodified Indigenous and African cultural symbols and practices, with the purpose of using as a marketing tool to make money. The successor to GVC, ",{"t":"a","c":["Mission School"],"id":"mission-school"}," is generally seen as more \"authentic\" in comparison."]},{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/33/GVC_Anasazi.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260304003330","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Packaging inspired by petroglyph art, Anasazi"]}," (mid 90s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/4/48/GVC_Levi%27s.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260304004132","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Advertisement inspired by petroglyph art, Levi's"]}," (1995)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/81/GVC_Avanti.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260304005211","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Kokopelli bathroom decor, Avanti Linens"]}," (2000s)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a4/GVC_Olive.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260304010611","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Kokopelli coffee, Olive Branch Coffee"]}," (2000s)"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/96/Digital_World.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192653","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Rafael Lopez"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1f/EyeInDaSky.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192730","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Rafael Lopez"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/9d/Pantone.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701180325","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Pantone poster"]}," (1989)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/0/0e/GVC2.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703012208","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Pantone poster"]}," (1989)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/88/GVC_Susan.webp/revision/latest?cb=20260324210911","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Susan Gross"]}," (1997)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6d/GVC14.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240703022209","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Art for Booz Allen & Hamilton by Smoking Gun Media"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/8/81/GVC_Jane.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260324214508","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Jane Mjolsness"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1c/Dancing.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192558","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["A palette heavy on CMYK colors, Art Deco influence, and use of stippled gradients generate a style halfway between GVC and ",{"t":"a","c":["Memphis Lite"],"id":"memphis-lite"},"."]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/35/Barcelona_92_poster.png/revision/latest?cb=20230523014247","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Barcelona Olympics advertisement"]}," (1992)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/de/Cocahits.png/revision/latest?cb=20240701180216","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Coca-Cola Partyhits compilation"]}," (1996)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/e/e0/GVC_WMTA.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260324212027","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["WMTA bus advertisement for summer concerts at Filene Center, Wolf Trap National Park, VA"]}," (1994)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/cb/TheCountyNews.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192421","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["NYC downtown summer events guide"]}," (2001)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/34/GVC5.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703013010","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Venice Way, designed by Trout Studios"]}," (1995)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/5/54/ThisIsn%E2%80%99tNintendo.png/revision/latest?cb=20230423221812","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Art from Nintendo annual report"]}," (1999)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/c8/GVC_Iowa_State.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20260324213957","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Iowa State University"]}," (1995)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/9/90/WINDOWS-CODENAME_MILLENIUM_GVCH.png/revision/latest?cb=20260515223844","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Windows Codename Millenium, Activity Center (Jump Theme)"]}," (1999)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a5/Undercover.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192501","w":140,"h":140},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/a/a3/CrapterNoons.jpeg/revision/latest?cb=20230424192630","w":140,"h":140},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/31/GVC13.png/revision/latest?cb=20240703060115","w":140,"h":140},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/3/37/GVC12.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240703013949","w":140,"h":140},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/b/b9/GVC_TLC.gif/revision/latest?cb=20260324212914","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["The Learning Channel (TLC)"]}]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6a/A_Little_Curious-_Stretch_Your_Imagination/revision/latest?cb=20251222233056","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Stretch Your Imagination from A Little Curious"]}," (1999)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/6d/How_Nehemiah_got_free_designed_by_Santiago_Cohen/revision/latest?cb=20260207174112","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["How Nehemiah Got Free"]}," (1998)"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/6/65/Troubles_the_Cat_S._1_episode_1_crayon_story_designed_by_Santiago_Cohen/revision/latest?cb=20260207174132","w":140,"h":140,"cap":[{"t":"i","c":["Crayon Story from Troubles the Cat"]}," (1996)"]}]}]}]}